zsh vi-mode
===========

Press ESC or ctrl-[ to enter normal mode.

HISTORY
  ctrl-p / ctrl-n      Previous / next command in history
  ctrl-r               Fuzzy search history with fzf (insert mode)
  /                    Search backward in history (normal mode)
  n                    Repeat the last /

EDIT IN THE EDITOR
  vv                   Edit the command line in $EDITOR (normal mode)

MOVEMENT
  0 / ^ / $            First character / first non-blank / end of the line
  w / W                [count] words / WORDS forward
  b / B                [count] words / WORDS backward
  e / E                Forward to the end of the word / WORD
  f{char} / F{char}    To the [count]th {char} to the right / left
  t{char} / T{char}    Till before the [count]th {char} to the right / left
  ; / ,                Repeat the last f, t, F or T / in the opposite direction

INSERT
  i / a                Insert before / append after the cursor
  I / A                Insert at the first character / append at the end of the line
  o / O                New command line below / above

DELETE AND CHANGE
  ctrl-h / ctrl-w      Insert mode: delete the character / word before the cursor
  d{motion} / dd / D   Delete over {motion} / the line / to the end of the line
  c{motion} / cc / C   Change over {motion} / the line / to the end of the line
  x / X                Delete [count] characters under / before the cursor
  r{char}              Replace the character under the cursor
  R                    Replace mode: each character replaces an existing one
